WEBVTT

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.860
The Trial Called Love

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.500
Beniya, we don't have enough.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.360
Can we really finish this 
with just three days to go?

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.590
I'm hungry. Let's send for a shopping run.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.870
Binan High School

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:49.230
The class or club that wins the 
popularity vote gets a cash prize, right?

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.850
Oh, that's right. That's what 
the Press Society guys said.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.710
Speaking of which, I heard the 
Press Society is broadcasting it.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.010
What do you mean, broadcasting?

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.630
<b>Binan High School Festival
Grand Prix</b>

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.630
<b>Who Will Win?!</b>

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.630
Like on the internet? Really?

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.770
Really!

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.760
Please allow our media to cover this!

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.910
<b>Earth Defense Club                         (lol)</b>

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.910
I told you, we should do a "how to date" class.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.990
No, we should have an 
investment awareness campaign.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:17.360
I don't really want to participate 
in this school festival stuff.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.380
I figured you'd say that, En-chan.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.880
It's such a pain in the ass, I want to die.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.380
What are you saying, Yufuin-senpai?

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.150
There's a cash prize on the line.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.830
Why wouldn't you pick up 
money just lying on the ground?

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.790
Bending over is a pain in the ass.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.140
He's hardcore lazy.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.210
But as long as we're being allotted 
a club room and club budget,

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:39.690
the student council says we have
to show the fruits of our activities.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.690
Here! Here! Here here here!

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.720
A restaurant! We should do a restaurant!

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.890
What is that, a kindergartner's dream?

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.480
No, that's a pretty realistic idea for Yumoto.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.650
Do you know the cost of coffee, for example?

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:55.690
What, is it easy money?

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.970
It also depends on our ability 
to draw customers, though.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:03:05.240
<b>In cold storage
Don't open!</b>

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.150
But everyone else is already gonna do 
stuff like cafés and coffee shops.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.340
That's true. It would be hard
without a selling point.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.870
We do have a selling point.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.250
We do?

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:10.560
Love Making!

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.690
The Thrilling Prince!

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.830
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.270
That we're transforming heroes!

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.590
No way.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:24.340
We've worked really hard to 
hide our identities up to now.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.840
Revealing them for something like 
this would make that all pointless.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.400
Well, that's different.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.160
Why don't we just get Wombat 
to work something out

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.270
with his advanced scientific technology?

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.250
Hey! Wait a minute!

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:41.530
It would be unheard of for missionaries 
of love to pursue for-profit ventures!

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.290
What are you saying?

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.030
If they eat delicious food, 
they'll feel love and happiness, right?

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:50.250
It's a proper love activity. A "lovetivity."

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.710
Lovetivity...

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.200
That's Ryuu for you.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.210
His sweet-talking technique is unsurpassed.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.970
Should you really be impressed by that?

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.780
I was just thinking it'd be nice 
to have a refrigerator, though.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.170
Why's that?

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.620
Well, we'd always have cold drinks on hand.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.420
A microwave would be great, too.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.930
Are you all really into this restaurant idea?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.220
Let's do it!

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:13.610
Lovetivity...

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.200
Coffee, black tea, and cake, maybe?

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.320
So it's decided that we're doing it, huh?

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.910
Love out.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.570
I think we should serve sushi.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.500
Nope.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:24.730
Why?

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.460
It takes too much work.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:29.040
And we'd be handling raw fish.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.370
It would be bad for us if 
any problems were to occur.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.270
Yeah. It's dangerous to serve 
stuff that isn't fully cooked.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.030
Curry would be good, then.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.870
This isn't just your decision, you know.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.640
"I would like curry," then.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.560
If we do curry, we could make it in 
the club room, then just heat it up.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.490
Atsushi makes good curry.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.470
I have to make it?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.870
Kinugawa Curry! Yeah!

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:54.980
I can't stand Thai curry, though.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.660
Why? Because it's spicy?

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.490
Actually, it's the coconut milk.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.130
I prefer thick home curry!

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.320
Dry curry is quite good, too.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.340
I like everything!

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.860
Exactly what kind of food is this "curry"?

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:17.930
I don't mind Thai curry, Atsushi-senpai.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.740
Pork is my favorite, though.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.590
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.320
Weren't you worrying about 
what kind of curry to make?

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:30.640
Because your face looked like this.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.590
What? When?

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.320
And I don't think I looked like that.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.650
Do you actually not like curry?

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.820
Gratin or napolitan would be fine, too!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:44.050
No... I do like curry, but...

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:45.180
I'm not sure...

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.860
What was it?

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.740
It gives you heartburn?

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.580
Maybe. Something about it just bothers me.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.750
Then you should take a bath and go to sleep.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.900
If you just take a bath,
most things will work themselves out!

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.340
That's what my big bro says.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:02.990
You're right. I guess I'll do that.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:07.010
<b>Binan Festival</b>

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.430
My Essays

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.790
<b>Honey Lemon</b>

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.110
When you make that expression,

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.820
it makes me start to feel melancholy, too.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.820
What kind of expression is that?

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.610
Like you've smelled something foul in the air.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:33.030
Now that you mention it...

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.420
I've been smelling curry for a while now.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.040
I don't understand people who eat curry.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.670
Doesn't everyone love curry?

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:45.720
Well, I suppose I wouldn't go 
out of my way to eat it, either.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:46.800
Why?

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.620
The dishes look less than 
beautiful after you eat it.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:51.600
That's not the problem!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.980
The powerful stench.
The stimulation against the tongue.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.830
It's not something civilized 
humans should be eating.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.610
You're that against it?

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.520
It's a thing we should object 
to on the most basic level.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.100
My, my.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.980
I don't know about such a radical way of thinking.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.520
As the rightful rulers of this planet,

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.720
we have the duty, the responsibility, and the right.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:16.240
By the way, I haven't seen Lord Zundar yet today.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.620
He's been going out a lot lately.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.660
Maybe it's mating season!

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.040
<b>Press Society</b>

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.040
<b>Binan High School Festival
Grand Prix</b>

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.040
<b>Who Will Win?!</b>

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:30.050
There's no denying you're in a rut.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:33.460
But I've been dedicated to 
devising clever schemes every week...

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.130
That's not good enough!

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.760
The masses get bored easily.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.750
I am aware of that.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:44.200
But anyway, this planet 
called Earth must be jinxed.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:48.150
I mean, we've conquered a lot of planets, right?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.840
Some of them have given 
us some trouble, of course.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:54.290
But we've conquered the 
vast majority of them, right?

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.640
And yet the Earth alone...

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:01.490
Why is this the only place 
where we've been canceled?

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.000
Canceled? What was the reason?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.600
Because it didn't go well.
An obstacle got in the way.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:09.570
Obstacle?

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:14.260
Still, I don't think the beings of this 
planet possess any special abilities.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.080
No, they do.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.840
Stupid power.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.130
They seem to call it "love," or some such...

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:24.440
It ain't love, stupid!

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.100
It's stupid power.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:31.070
So what kind of soldiers do we need 
to oppose this "stupid love power"?

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:36.040
Good question. We might need 
an even more negative person.

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:37.960
Negative?

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:43.540
Yeah. Someone soggy, viscous, 
and goopy who will really stick with it.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:47.420
A human steeped in grudge and discontent.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.180
Big bro, what's wrong?

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.630
You don't have your usual edge.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:55.850
I-It's nothing.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.550
Hey, there's something I want to ask you.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.050
The other day, when you...

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.510
You mean the "first cold in my life" incident?

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:07.440
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.690
I don't remember it very well.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.590
I was carrying a cleaning rag.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:14.490
A cleaning rag?

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.800
Yeah. And for some reason, I had glasses.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:17.640
Glasses?

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.280
And a baseball.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:20.450
Really?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.410
I think. Sorry if I'm wrong.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.470
So what was it you wanted to ask me?

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:28.680
Well, Yumoto...

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:31.000
What do you think of transformation...

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.040
Deviation and such?

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.200
Deviation?

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:37.430
<i>Has he discovered some weird hobby?</i>

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.350
Well, I think it's fine!

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:43.040
People are free to do as they like.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.930
As long as they aren't bothering 
others, I'd encourage them.

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:48.180
I see.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:51.800
Did he want me to stop him?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.410
Let's eat!

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:03.120
Eat!

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:08.880
It's good!

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.960
Curry's so good! Good curry!

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.930
Shut up and eat.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:17.420
But don't you think the Kinugawa Curry is good?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:19.880
It's not about that. It's because you're annoying.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.680
I'm more fascinated

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.600
by the surrealism of Wombat eating curry.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.930
Human know-how produces 
such a condensed taste!

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:31.890
300 yen for a plate of curry.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:34.570
And if we factor in the cash prize...

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.530
Wow, you seem confident we'll win.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.650
Of course I am.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:40.660
Can we start now, then?

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.800
Love Making into the Battle Lovers!

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.990
Love Making!

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.920
The Sparkling Prince!

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.360
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.350
Love Making!

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.660
The Flashing Prince!

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.870
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:32.810
Love Making!

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:42.790
The Piercing Prince!

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:45.390
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.420
Love Making!

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.340
The Roaring Prince!

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:59.900
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:02.010
Love Making!

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:11.980
The Thrilling Prince!

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.410
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:17.210
You, who befoul our beloved Earth!

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.960
No justice can come from loveless power!

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.210
Love is all!

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.720
Live for love! Die for love!

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:27.850
We are the heirs to the throne of love!

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:29.350
Battle Lovers!

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:31.120
Feel the power...

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:33.550
Of love!

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.730
You really don't think they'll realize

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:41.040
that we're the same people as those guys?

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.620
The blur isn't on us, right?

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.660
Will that be okay?

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:49.590
It's fine. My highly advanced scientific 
technology has mumble mumble...

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.590
What do you mean, "mumble mumble"?

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:54.000
Now, let's go get customers!

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:59.880
<b>Zundar
Born August 18th 
(converted to Earth calendar)
Blood Type B / Leo
Hobbies: Secret
Likes: Escargot</b>

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:02.650
Deliciousness that shakes the Earth!

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:04.220
Even an alien would be shocked!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.920
Why are you dressed like that, Hakone?

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.270
We're transforming heroes!

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:10.600
You know, we've seen them around 
the school a lot lately, right?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.900
That weird group of five.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:13.770
We're cosplaying as them!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.340
It's not a lie, I guess.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:17.770
And yet, it's a perfect cover story.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.430
Yumoto's amazing.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:22.950
Cosplay Hero Curry! Now on sale!

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:26.900
Cosplays, heroes, and curry? 
Isn't that a bit too much at once?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.120
Put on more! More and more and more!

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:32.210
We don't have a choice. 
I guess we'd better work, too.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:33.760
I don't want to have any leftovers.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:34.610
Sure.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:35.600
Let's go.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.730
Atsushi, you handle the curry stock.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:38.610
Roger.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:41.040
Give me something to do, too!

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:44.510
Wombat, you and Mr. Tawarayama watch the store.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.390
I accept!

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.210
Defense curry.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:53.820
It's good.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:54.640
Okay.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.350
A little more enthusiasm.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:59.690
Why do I have to suffer such poor treatment?

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.940
Mr. Tawarayama can't help 
unless both his hands are free.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:04.570
Defense Club Curry 300 yen

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.460
Even so...

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.100
Well, you can't go away from him.

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:07.640
But...

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.030
Sir, you're not doing any work.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.610
It's still got an edge to it.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:19.320
Oops.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:25.630
Foolish humans who lack ambition 
or aspiration have no right to exist.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.420
They are worthless.

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:34.150
I will purge ugly things, foolish things, 
and worthless things from the world.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:38.770
The world should be orderly, beautiful, and regular.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.190
And yet, what is this curry stench?

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.950
Why is it drifting in from over here?

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:55.800
Um...

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:57.210
Want some?

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:00.790
Who would stoop to eating something so humble?!

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:07.760
Kin-chan?

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.810
Do not call me by that name.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.770
Kin-chan, you're our enemy? That can't be true.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.310
Truly base and vulgar.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:23.230
Its wicked stimulation poisons the sense 
of taste and destroys the sense of smell.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:27.200
Worse, its offensive appearance 
mocks the sense of sight.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:31.160
I cannot fathom a person like you 
who can this thing known as curry,

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.140
Kinugawa Atsushi.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.400
No. My name is...

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.830
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:45.300
I see. So our battle was fated, then!

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.040
Go, Aurite!

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.770
The time has come to unleash your power

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:51.680
and achieve your longstanding desire!

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.140
Conquest!

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:02.450
My name is Dark Aurite.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.600
The Black Chevalier, writhing in darkness!

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.530
Ater Aurum!

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:14.930
What's that?

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:16.710
That's where the student council room is.

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:17.790
What's that?

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.420
That's where our club room is.

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.620
Wait! Let's do this after the culture festival's over!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.800
I want to sell the curry I worked so hard to make!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.060
Curry, you say?

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:33.730
Just leave it to rot!

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:37.700
No! That curry's important to me!

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.260
Why? Why curry, of all things?

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.980
If we're talking about "of all things,"

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.560
why do you have to be my
enemy of all things, Kin-chan?

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.280
Don't call me by that name!

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:52.950
Wow! Who's putting on that performance?

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.400
Cool! There's lights and everything!

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.100
What's going on?

00:16:57.100 --> 00:17:00.080
It must be serious, to make 
the president forget himself.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.570
Why is Atsushi fighting?

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:04.710
President?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:05.920
Atsushi?

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:09.800
Why can we see their faces?

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:13.340
The blur isn't on us, right?

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.010
Mumble mumble, and all.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.730
You guys are...

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:19.380
Caerula Adamas?

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:20.980
The Battle Lovers?

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:22.440
Um...

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.720
Conquest!

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:28.570
The Silver Chevalier, rustling young leaves!

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:29.960
Argent!

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:35.720
The Pearl Chevalier, making flowers bloom!

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:37.070
Perlite!

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:42.240
A bad omen.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.500
How dare you deceive us all this time?!

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:47.670
That's our line!

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:52.630
Learning your identities is 
a real load off our minds!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.600
It's hard to see something that's 
right under your nose, I guess!

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:00.690
What's going to happen to the curry?

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:03.390
What about the profits from Cosplay Hero Curry?

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:04.970
Mumble mumble, I'd say!

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.480
Gigant Aurum!

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:14.990
Yumo—

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.390
Why are you two fighting?!

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.660
This is not such a trivial thing!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.520
But it <i>is</i> a fight, isn't it?

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:25.500
He just hates me, that's all.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.670
That's right.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.330
I hate you, Kinugawa Atsushi.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:32.430
Ever since that day you rejected me!

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:36.210
Rejected? What did you do, Atsushi-senpai?

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:40.100
Rejected? Did I do that to you, Kin-chan?

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:42.350
If you're playing dumb, it's pathetic.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:46.100
If you really have forgotten, 
then I'll consign you to death!

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:49.220
At-chan, you're coming by my house, right?

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.530
I can't today. I've got something to do.

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:53.530
Okay...

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.680
Whoops.

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.200
Th-Thanks.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.040
Kinugawa? Where are you going?

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.290
CoCoKaRa Curry.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:07.080
That's right. Today's their extra-spicy curry day.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.870
Yufuin, you like curry?

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:09.550
Pretty well.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:11.040
Want to go with me?

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:13.550
I have a coupon.

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:15.920
All curry 20% off

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:15.580
So do I.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.210
If I had to choose which I hate more, 
mild curry or stinky natto,

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:20.260
I'd choose mild curry any time.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:24.280
That's right. There are people 
who find even the mild stuff spicy.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.350
Stupid curry.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:30.940
Morning, Kin-chan.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:38.020
Kin-chan?

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:42.770
What, did you have a fight or something?

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:44.710
I don't remember having one...

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.560
What, you're fighting and 
you don't even know why?

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:50.050
Why not ask him?

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:51.960
I'd better not.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:55.360
If he doesn't want to talk about it,
I'd feel bad trying to force it out of him.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.970
You broke our oath!

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:00.180
Oath?

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.760
What did you wish for?

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:10.140
I wished for us to stay friends forever.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:13.690
You don't need to wish on a shooting star for that.

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:19.420
'Cause we'll be friends forever, no matter what.

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.660
You stomped on decorum!

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.370
Yumoto...

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:32.660
I'm coming now.

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:39.880
Don't get in my way!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:42.530
Please don't have a falling-out in front of me!

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:44.350
I hate that kind of thing!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.060
In that case...

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:50.740
I'll destroy you both together!

00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:57.000
<i>Do they intend to do the same thing again?</i>

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.050
Fight!

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:06.450
One shot?

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:08.420
Hey, you're late!

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:11.500
En-chan!

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.330
Sorry I'm late.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:22.720
When I hear that story of yours, Kusatsu, 
it sounds to me like you're just sulking!

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:24.430
Shut up, you coward!

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:28.100
We won't stand silent while you 
slander the good name of curry!

00:21:43.090 --> 00:21:46.940
It's presumptuous to think that 
the likes of you could oppose us.

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:50.780
If you withdraw now, we won't harm you.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:54.740
I am going to stop this stupid fight between you!

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:57.170
Oh? It's being drawn out that long?

00:21:57.170 --> 00:22:00.220
That's great. Just what I wanted.

00:23:39.870 --> 00:23:43.580
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:43.630 --> 00:23:47.340
<b>At Last</b>

00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:51.090
<b>The Final Episode!</b>
